# Rules before the first `user` line apply to every client, which here means
# every anonymous one: the students. They may read the plant and nothing else.
# In particular they may not publish, so no one can inject a fabricated
# reading into the stream somebody else is collecting.
topic read plant/#

# The simulator is the one client that writes, and it is the only reason the
# broker has a password file at all. Anonymous read plus one authenticated
# writer is the whole access-control design.
user tep-publisher
topic write plant/#
